# Data Pipeline Rules

## Independence
The data pipeline is a distinct, independently runnable component. Client apps (`apps/*`) must NOT
depend on it at build time. Output is ingested into Supabase via batch import scripts.

## Scraping Etiquette
- Respect `robots.txt` on target sites.
- Implement retry with exponential backoff (base 2s, max 60s, 5 retries).
- Rotate proxies when rate-limited (configurable proxy pool in `data-pipeline/config/`).
- Rate limit: max 1 request/second per domain unless robots.txt permits more.
- User-Agent: identify as `GTR-Auto-CatalogBot/1.0 (+https://nissangtrauto.co.zw/bot)`.
- Cache responses locally to avoid re-scraping unchanged pages.

## Nissan FAST EPC Parsing
- Hierarchy: Model Variant → Engine/Chassis Code → Sub-Assembly → Diagram.
- VIN prefix decoding → chassis_code, engine_code, production_year.
- 5-digit PNC codes → category/subcategory mapping.
- 10-digit OEM part numbers with supersession chain (`superseded_by`).

## Catalog Asset Pipeline
- Scrape diagram images (PNG/JPG) from reference sites (Amayama, 7zap, PartSouq).
- Extract X/Y/width/height bounding-box coordinates as JSON.
- Store base images in Supabase Storage; spatial data in Postgres (`part_fitment`).

## Output Schema
All pipeline output must conform to the JSON schema in `data-pipeline/schemas/`:
- `vehicle_master.schema.json`
- `pnc_categories.schema.json`
- `part_fitment.schema.json`
- `diagram_assets.schema.json`

Validate output with `jsonschema` before import.

## Indexing
Push aggregated hierarchy into Meilisearch (or configured search index) after import.
Support 4-way search: part number, VIN, model variant, PNC category.

## Python Conventions
- Python 3.11+. Use `playwright` for JS-rendered pages, `beautifulsoup4` for static HTML.
- Type hints on all functions. `ruff` for linting, `pytest` for tests.
- Run via `python -m data_pipeline.<module>` — no implicit `__main__` side effects.
